### Correr con: dotnet run --project src/Orders  (perfil http: puerto 44050)
@host = http://localhost:44050

### 1. Pedido normal -> lo procesa el consumer y publica OrderProcessed (solo lo ve "all-orders")
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "ana", "product": "book", "amount": 50 }

### 2. Pedido grande -> lo ven las DOS subscriptions ("high-value" filtra amount > 1000)
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "bruno", "product": "laptop", "amount": 2500 }

### 3. Duplicate detection: mandalo DOS veces seguidas con el mismo id -> el broker descarta la segunda
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111", "customer": "carla", "product": "pen", "amount": 5 }

### 4. Pedido inválido -> dead-letter explícito con motivo, sin reintentos
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "dani", "product": "mouse", "amount": 0 }

### 5. Falla transitoria -> 3 intentos (MaxDeliveryCount) y termina en la DLQ sola
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "eli", "product": "flaky", "amount": 30 }

### 6. Ver la DLQ (peek, no consume)
GET {{host}}/dlq

### 7. Reprocesar la DLQ (el "flaky" ahora pasa; el inválido vuelve a la DLQ)
POST {{host}}/dlq/replay
